-- Step 28: shipments, import charges and landed cost.
-- track: B
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A shipment gathers the posted goods received notes of one consignment from a supplier, with
-- what identifies it at the port and how far it has come. It takes its SH number as it is
-- opened. The charges of bringing it in are lines of posted supplier bills charged to Goods in
-- transit (freight, duty, clearing, tax paid at import, a container deposit); each is put on
-- the shipment with what kind of charge it is. Nothing reaches the books until the charges are
-- spread, with app.allocate_shipment, which closes the shipment:
--
--   debit   Stock in trade                    charges that are part of what the goods cost,
--                                             for the goods still held
--   debit   Cost of goods sold                the same, for goods that have already gone
--   debit   Sales tax receivable (input tax)  sales tax paid at import
--   debit   Advance income tax                income tax paid at import
--   debit   the account named                 a deposit, or an expense
--   credit  Goods in transit                  every charge, as its bill charged it
--
-- A charge that is part of what the goods cost is spread over the lines of the shipment's
-- goods by value, quantity, weight or volume, to the paisa. For each item, the part of the
-- shipment's quantity that the company still holds (in any warehouse) takes its share into
-- stock, which raises what each unit is carried at; the rest goes to cost of goods sold. A
-- charge that comes after the shipment was closed is spread the same way, on its own, when
-- app.allocate_shipment is called again: it adjusts the stock still held and the cost of the
-- units already sold.
--
-- Stock is revalued with a move that has a value and no quantity (app.revalue_stock), so the
-- two checks on stock_moves that asked every move for a quantity are relaxed for that case.
--
-- A bill line may now be charged to Goods in transit: app.check_supplier_bill_line (Step 25,
-- this track's) is written out again below with that one change.
--
-- The owner and an accountant open shipments, put goods and charges on them and spread the
-- charges; the auditor reads. The app's role cannot write a shipment's number or status, what
-- a charge amounts to, that a charge was spread, or anything of the spreading.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE200 to SE299 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 30 used SE200
-- to SE210, Step 24 SE211 to SE222, Step 25 SE223 to SE234, Step 26 SE235 to SE245 and
-- Step 27 SE246 to SE254:
--   SE255  no such shipment in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE256  the shipment is not in the state this needs
--   SE257  a shipment is never removed, and what it is never changes
--   SE258  the goods of a shipment are posted goods received notes from its supplier into its
--          branch, each on one shipment, put on or taken off only while the shipment is open
--   SE259  a charge is a line of a posted bill of the shipment's branch charged to Goods in
--          transit, with an account that suits its kind
--   SE260  there is no charge waiting to be spread
--   SE261  the shipment has no goods to spread charges over
--   SE262  a charge cannot be spread by a measure none of the goods has
--   SE263  a date that has not come yet, is no day on the calendar, or is before the goods
--          arrived or a charge was billed
--   SE264  a shipment with goods or charges on it is not cancelled
--   SE265  what has been spread is never changed or removed
--   SE266  stock that is not held cannot be revalued, nor below nothing
-- SE219 (purchase documents are written in read committed transactions) is Step 24's, used again.

